.TH BUNDLEINFO 1
.SH NAME
bundleinfo \\- inventory macOS application and package bundles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bundleinfo
bundleinfo PATH
.SH DESCRIPTION
Inspects .app and .pkg structure and metadata without executing bundle content.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBbundleinfo --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
